---

<Docs
  title="CLI Reference"
  description="All astro-doctor CLI commands, flags, and examples."
  editPath="apps/docs/src/pages/docs/cli.astro"
>
  <header class="docs-page-header">
    <h1>CLI reference</h1>
    <p class="docs-page-lead">
      Scan a project, control which findings matter, and export a report from your terminal.
    </p>
  </header>

  <CodeBlock
    code="astro-doctor [command] [options]"
    language="bash"
    theme="auto"
    variant="block"
    copy
  />

  <h2>Commands</h2>

  <h3>(no command) — scan</h3>

  <p>Scans the target directory for Astro issues and prints a health report.</p>

  <CodeBlock
    code={`# Scan current directory
astro-doctor

# Scan a specific directory
astro-doctor --dir ./src

# Scan and write a JSON report
astro-doctor --json report.json

# Emit SARIF for code-scanning tools
astro-doctor --format sarif > astro-doctor.sarif

# Apply safe automatic fixes
astro-doctor --fix

# Preview safe fixes without writing source files
astro-doctor --fix-dry-run

# Explain configuration for a file
astro-doctor explain-config src/pages/index.astro

# Cache repeated scans by file content
astro-doctor --cache

# Save and apply a persistent baseline
astro-doctor baseline create
astro-doctor --baseline .astro-doctor-baseline.json

# Report only diagnostics introduced since main
astro-doctor --scope changed --base main

# Scan without showing the health score
astro-doctor --no-score`}
    language="bash"
    theme="auto"
    variant="block"
    copy
  />

  <h3><code>install</code></h3>

  <p>
    Writes the portable skill to <code>skills/astro-doctor.md</code> and offers GitHub Actions
    setup. Use <code>--agent-hooks</code> for Claude Code and Cursor copies,
    <code>--dry-run</code> to preview changes, or <code>--yes</code> to accept the setup prompts.
  </p>

  <CodeBlock code="astro-doctor install" language="bash" />

  <h3><code>baseline create|update|prune</code></h3>

  <p>
    Saves the current findings to <code>.astro-doctor-baseline.json</code>. Subsequent scans with
    <code>--baseline</code> report only findings that are not already recorded, making gradual
    adoption practical in existing projects. Reports include new and existing finding counts;
    resolved counts are shown only for full, unfiltered scans. Resolved means no longer reported
    under the current configuration, including findings in deleted files.
  </p>

  <CodeBlock
    code={`astro-doctor baseline create
astro-doctor baseline update --output ./config/astro-baseline.json
astro-doctor baseline prune
astro-doctor baseline prune --output ./config/astro-baseline.json`}
    language="bash"
    theme="auto"
    variant="block"
    copy
  />

  <p>
    <code>baseline prune</code> removes only recorded occurrences no longer reported, retaining
    the original timestamp and never accepting new findings. It requires a full scan and rejects
    file scopes, category filters, explicit project selections, fix flags, and
    <code>--no-lint</code>. Astro parse failures block baseline comparisons and leave the baseline unchanged. Run pruning with the same
    preset and configuration used to create the baseline; disabling a rule also removes its findings.
  </p>

  <h3><code>explain-config &lt;file&gt;</code></h3>

  <p>
    Shows the scan preset, effective template rule severities, matching ignore patterns, and
    zero-based override indexes in application order. Workspace files use the same root and project
    configuration layering as scans. Project audit rules appear separately because template file
    overrides do not affect them. Inline suppression comments are evaluated during linting and are
    not part of this configuration report.
  </p>

  <CodeBlock
    code={`astro-doctor explain-config src/pages/index.astro
astro-doctor explain-config src/pages/index.astro --preset strict --json`}
    language="bash"
    copy
  />

  <h3><code>--fix-dry-run</code></h3>

  <p>
    Simulates the same safe fixes as <code>--fix</code> and prints unified diffs, the net count of
    findings removed, and remaining findings. Source files and the ESLint cache stay unchanged.
    Diagnostic counts, scores, and failure gates describe the simulated result. JSON reports include
    an optional <code>fixPreview</code> object; baseline reports include
    <code>baselineProgress</code>, with <code>resolvedCount</code> omitted for partial scans.
    Combining previews with a baseline shows projected progress after fixes.
    Use console or JSON output without category filters, <code>--score</code>,
    <code>--fix</code>, or <code>--no-lint</code>.
  </p>

  <h3><code>experimental-lsp</code></h3>

  <p>
    Starts the experimental language server in stdio mode (for editor integration without ESLint).
    This feature is a work in progress.
  </p>

  <CodeBlock
    code="astro-doctor experimental-lsp --stdio"
    language="bash"
    theme="auto"
    variant="block"
    copy
  />

  <h2>Options</h2>

  <Table aria-label="CLI options" role="region" tabindex="0">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Flag</th>
          <th>Default</th>
          <th>Description</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td><code>-d, --dir &lt;path&gt;</code></td>
          <td><code>process.cwd()</code></td>
          <td>Directory to scan</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>--scope &lt;scope&gt;</code></td>
          <td><code>full</code></td>
          <td>Choose <code>full</code>, changed <code>files</code>, or introduced diagnostics with <code>changed</code></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>--base &lt;ref&gt;</code></td>
          <td>auto-detected</td>
          <td>Base revision for <code>files</code> or <code>changed</code> scope</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>--json [path]</code></td>
          <td><em>off</em></td>
          <td>Output JSON to stdout (no path) or to a file</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>--fix</code></td>
          <td><em>off</em></td>
          <td>Apply safe automatic fixes provided by rules</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>--preset &lt;name&gt;</code></td>
          <td><code>recommended</code></td>
          <td><code>recommended</code> | <code>strict</code> | <code>ci</code> | <code>all</code></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>--fix-dry-run</code></td>
          <td><em>off</em></td>
          <td>Preview safe fixes and remaining findings without source or cache writes</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>--cache</code></td>
          <td><em>off</em></td>
          <td>Cache ESLint results by file content at <code>.astro-doctor/cache</code>; add it to <code>.gitignore</code></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>--baseline &lt;path&gt;</code></td>
          <td><em>off</em></td>
          <td>Suppress findings recorded in a persistent baseline</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>--format &lt;format&gt;</code></td>
          <td><code>console</code></td>
          <td>Choose <code>console</code>, <code>github</code>, or <code>sarif</code></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>--no-score</code></td>
          <td><em>show score</em></td>
          <td>Omit the health score from output</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>--fail-on &lt;level&gt;</code></td>
          <td><code>error</code></td>
          <td>Exit 1 on: <code>error</code> | <code>warning</code> | <code>off</code></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>--changed-files-from &lt;path&gt;</code></td>
          <td><em>off</em></td>
          <td>Scan only files listed in a file (one path per line) — used by the GitHub Action for PR diff mode</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>-h, --help</code></td>
          <td>—</td>
          <td>Show help message</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </Table>

  <h2>JSON report schema</h2>

  <p>When using <code>--json</code>, the output conforms to this schema:</p>

  <CodeBlock
    code={`{
  "$schema": "https://doctor.santi020k.com/schema/report.json",
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "version": "1.x.x",
  "scoreModel": 2,
  "timestamp": "2024-01-01T00:00:00.000Z",
  "directory": "/my-project",
  "scope": "full",
  "fileCount": 14,
  "errorCount": 1,
  "warningCount": 0,
  "score": 89,
  "scoreLabel": "B",
  "scoreBreakdown": {
    "performance": 100,
    "accessibility": 89,
    "security": 100,
    "best-practices": 100
  },
  "diagnostics": [
    {
      "ruleId": "astro-doctor/no-missing-alt",
      "severity": "error",
      "message": "Image elements must have an alt attribute. Provide a descriptive text for meaningful images, or alt=\\"\\" for decorative ones.",
      "filePath": "/my-project/src/pages/blog.astro",
      "line": 12,
      "column": 5,
      "category": "accessibility"
    }
  ]
}`}
    language="json"
    theme="auto"
    variant="block"
    copy
  />

  <h2>Exit codes</h2>

  <Table aria-label="CLI exit codes" role="region" tabindex="0">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Code</th>
          <th>Meaning</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td><code>0</code></td>
          <td>Scan completed, no issues at or above the fail-on threshold</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>1</code></td>
          <td>Issues found at or above the fail-on threshold</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </Table>

  <h2>Examples</h2>

  <CodeBlock
    code={`# CI: fail on any warning
astro-doctor --fail-on warning

# CI: never fail, just report
astro-doctor --fail-on off

# Output JSON for downstream tools
astro-doctor --json | jq '.score'

# Write JSON to a file and show console output
astro-doctor --json ./astro-report.json`}
    language="bash"
    theme="auto"
    variant="block"
    copy
  />
</Docs>
